ITEM 1 - sink sets and demand correlation  [HEADLINE]
========================================================================================================
  Two sign conventions, both reported to avoid ambiguity:
    rho_rank = spearman(demand RANK, sink indicator)   NEGATIVE = sinks are high-demand (good)
    rho_val  = spearman(demand c,    sink indicator)   POSITIVE = sinks are high-demand (good)

  operator  sinks/g  mean rank P(sink|top10) P(sink|bot10)    rho_rank     rho_val
  LAP           3.6       30.2         9.0%         1.0%      -0.097       0.098
  RANK         13.3       25.5        46.6%         0.7%      -0.290       0.289
  (all-node mean rank is 40.5)

  For reference, from flow-orientation.md: FLOW rho_rank = +0.132 (anti-correlated),
  TREE rho_rank = +0.040 / -0.048 / -0.085.

